COMMAND TRANSCRIPT — consumer-owned size prop triggers style-token warning

Expectation from docs/primitives.mdx: a prop read by the component for itself,
such as size turned into data-size, stays the component's own prop.

Minimal fixture: repro/consumed-size-prop.tsx contains LocalButton reading size
and rendering Button data-size={size}; it never forwards a size style prop.
The same data-size behavior using buttonSize is a passing control.

Temporarily set ui.config.ts include to ['repro/consumed-size-prop.tsx'].
$ npm run sync -- --verbose
Exit: 0, but warning:

repro/consumed-size-prop.tsx:8:42 ATM-W-UNKNOWN-TOKEN: `lg` is not a size token x2
— use a size token or a CSS value

REF v0.0.0 ready in 306 ms
CSS: 164.3 KB

No warning is emitted for the renamed buttonSize control.

$ npm exec -- tsc --noEmit --strict --skipLibCheck \
    --moduleResolution bundler --module esnext --target es2022 \
    --jsx react-jsx repro/consumed-size-prop.tsx
Exit: 0; no TypeScript diagnostics.

Restored the demo include glob after the isolated sync. Original compiler log
is preserved in logs/consumed-size-prop-minimal-sync.log.
